  "community-apocalypse-terrace": {"sourcePromptAvailable":true,"sourceAuditStatus":"verified-2026-11-05","sourceTitle":"Apocalypse Terrace","sourceRecordId":"37996bac-c100-40b4-81a8-c0f024c75a7c","sourceVariantId":"f0fad1a9-2a7e-4675-9a99-8d781cf04737","sourceMediaId":"cba9c45e-2ac1-49eb-b6ac-e33cee614708","prompt":"Create a photorealistic cinematic video that follows the supplied reference video as closely as possible in shot sequence, pacing, camera angles, composition, actions, emotional tone and visual rhythm.\n\nUse the uploaded portrait as the identity reference for the main character. Keep his face, hairstyle, body proportions, age, skin tone and overall identity consistent throughout the entire clip. Do not change his facial structure.\n\nThe video should feel like a nearly shot-for-shot recreation of the reference video, but with this man as the main character.\n\nSCENE OVERVIEW:\nA calm, elegant, cinematic seaside terrace scene at sunset. The mood is luxurious, quiet and emotionally restrained, while an apocalyptic disaster unfolds in the background.\n\nSHOT-BY-SHOT STRUCTURE:\n\nShot 1:\nStart with a calm, cinematic side-profile shot of the man sitting in a wooden or elegant outdoor lounge chair on a minimalist luxury terrace overlooking the ocean at sunset. He is seated comfortably and relaxed. He is reading a newspaper or magazine. The background is peaceful at first, with the sea and glowing sunset sky visible.\n\nShot 2:\nA nuke appears in the sky behind him, moving slowly across the horizon toward the ocean. The nuke must be big, highly realistic and visually dramatic, with smoke trails and sparks. It should feel threatening and catastrophic.\n\nThe man remains completely calm and still. He does not panic. He continues sitting relaxed as if nothing unusual is happening.\n\nShot 3:\nAs the nuke continues descending in the background, the man slowly lowers the tablet. His movement is subtle, controlled and elegant.\n\nHis emotional expression is important:\nHe looks calm, stoic and composed. One or two subtle tears may roll down his cheeks. He is not sobbing. He is not making exaggerated expressions. The sadness should feel quiet, controlled, cinematic and deeply human.\n\nShot 4:\nCut to a close-up insert shot of his hand reaching toward a small side table next to the lounge chair. On the table is a cold bottle of Nuka Cola like in . His hand slowly and naturally picks up the bottle.\n\nShot 5:\nCut back to a medium side-profile shot. The nuke is still descending behind him. He slowly lifts the bottle toward his mouth.\n\nHis eyes remain emotional, with visible tears, but he stays completely composed. His facial expression remains subtle and restrained.\n\nShot 6:\nHe takes a slow sip from the drink while the nuke crashes into the ocean in the far background.\n\nThe impact is massive and cinematic:\nA huge fiery explosion erupts on the horizon, followed by enormous plumes of smoke, steam, glowing debris, water spray and a shockwave. The explosion must feel physically believable and visually epic.\n\nShot 7:\nThe camera widens. The man is still seated quietly, holding the bottle, completely calm despite the catastrophe.\n\nA gigantic tsunami wave begins to rise in the distance behind him. The wave grows rapidly, becoming enormous and overwhelming, filling more and more of the frame as it approaches the terrace.\n\nShot 8:\nFinal wide cinematic shot. The wave is now towering behind him and dominates the background. The man remains seated, calm, dignified and motionless, holding his drink with subtle tears still visible in his eyes. The emotional contrast between his quiet sadness and the apocalyptic destruction creates a surreal, darkly funny, cinematic ending.\n\nCHARACTER PERFORMANCE:\nThe man must remain calm, stoic and emotionally contained throughout the entire clip.\nHis tears should be realistic and restrained.\nHe should appear quietly moved or touched, with watery eyes and one or two tears, but never exaggerated.\nNo dramatic crying, no sobbing, no screaming, no overacting.\n\nVISUAL STYLE:\nUltra-realistic, photorealistic, cinematic, premium, elegant and emotionally powerful.\nGolden sunset lighting.\nLuxury terrace atmosphere.\nHigh-end film look.\nNatural skin texture.\nRealistic facial animation.\nRealistic hair and clothing movement.\nRealistic ocean, fire, smoke, explosion and tsunami physics.\nSubtle depth of field.\nClean, expensive color grading.\nQuiet, polished, blockbuster-quality imagery.\n\nCAMERA STYLE:\nUse calm, elegant cinematic camera language similar to the reference video.\nSlow controlled camera movement.\nNatural cuts between side-profile shot, hand close-up, medium shot and wide final shot.\nNo shaky cam.\nNo chaotic editing.\nNo fast action camera.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nMatch the supplied reference video as closely as possible in structure, sequence and mood.\nPreserve the man’s exact identity from the uploaded portrait.\nKeep the tears subtle and realistic.\nNo face distortion.\nNo identity drift.\nNo extra fingers.\nNo extra people.\nNo text.\nNo logos.\nNo cartoon style.\nNo surreal face warping.\nNo exaggerated acting.\nNo goofy expressions."},
